racc's C extension is a pure accelerator: the same gem carries a complete
Ruby runtime behind `rescue LoadError`. Loading any C extension arms the
GVL process-wide (attr_accessor +68%, getivar +65% on the release bank),
so zeo declines the cparse build and the gem's own rescue takes the Ruby
runtime, which zeo compiles to native code. The oracle, with the built
extension in its store, answers "c"; zeo answers "ruby". Every parse
answers the same either way -- a_racc_parser_answers_the_same_off_either
_runtime.rb is the parity half of this pair.
